// pipl — China's Personal Information Protection Law
//
// The law: critical information infrastructure operators, and processors
// handling personal information above the thresholds the CAC sets, must
// store it in China; anyone sending it abroad needs a security assessment,
// certification or the CAC's standard contract (Arts. 38–40).
//
// This pack: everything runs in China.
//
// Use `import "pipl"`. Not legal advice.

policy pipl {
  residency = china
}
